<h2>The pricing question</h2>

<p>On paper, ActiveCampaign looks cheaper. The Starter plan at $29 per month undercuts DUSA's pricing. But that comparison only works if email is the only thing you need.</p>

<p>In practice, a small business owner who needs email automation, a funnel builder, SMS, booking, and review management will spend $149 per month on ActiveCampaign Pro, plus $30 to $50 per month on a landing page builder, $15 to $30 per month on a booking tool, and $50 or more per month on a review platform. The total easily reaches $250 to $350 per month across four or five separate subscriptions.</p>

<p>DUSA includes all of that from $97 per month. The pricing comparison is not really DUSA versus ActiveCampaign. It is DUSA versus ActiveCampaign plus Calendly plus Leadpages plus Podium plus an SMS provider.</p>

<h2>When ActiveCampaign is the better choice</h2>

<p>ActiveCampaign is the better choice if email automation is your number one priority and you need the most advanced workflow builder available. If you are an e-commerce brand sending highly segmented campaigns with conditional logic, predictive content, and split testing across dozens of segments, ActiveCampaign was built for that level of email sophistication.</p>

<p>It also makes sense if you already have your other tools sorted. If you are happy with your current landing page builder, booking system, and review platform, and you just need a best-in-class email engine to plug into that stack, ActiveCampaign fills that role well.</p>

<h2>When DUSA is the better choice</h2>

<p>DUSA is the better choice if you are a sole operator or small team that needs more than email. If you want one platform that handles your CRM, your email marketing, your SMS, your funnels, your bookings, and your reviews, DUSA gives you that without stitching together five different subscriptions.</p>

<p>It is also the better choice if you value simplicity. Running a small business is complex enough without managing logins, billing, and integrations across half a dozen tools. DUSA consolidates the stack so you can focus on the work that actually grows your business. For a wider look at why consolidation makes sense, our <a href="/blog/all-in-one-vs-separate-tools">all-in-one vs separate tools comparison</a> breaks it down.</p>

<blockquote><p>The best email platform in the world does not help much if you still need four other tools to run your business.</p></blockquote>

<div class="divider">...</div>

<h2>The bottom line</h2>

<p>ActiveCampaign and DUSA solve overlapping problems, but they serve different needs. ActiveCampaign is a specialist. It does email automation at a level that few platforms can match, and it has earned its place as a leader in that category.</p>

<p>DUSA is a platform. It covers email automation along with everything else a small business needs to grow. The email features are strong, but they are part of a bigger picture that includes funnels, bookings, SMS, reviews, and CRM.</p>

<p>If email automation complexity is the thing that matters most to you, ActiveCampaign is hard to beat. If you need a complete growth platform that handles email and everything else, DUSA is the more practical and more affordable choice.</p>

